  "id": "native-subtype-c-cpp-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "8ff62bf224300418a4748dd3209bb607e963f140",
  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_SUBTYPE_PROFILES=c,cpp node --test tests/native-subtype.test.mjs",
  "scope": "Two clean roots reproduce the C and C++ archives for ordinary-source exports whose top-level parameters and results are Subtypes over String, Nat, Int and ByteArray with contract-named checked constructors: a nonempty string argument and result, an even Nat, a bounded Int after an unchecked Int, a nonempty ByteArray, a result-only even Nat, two checked strings, a normalizing constructor that clamps to 100, and an even Nat beside a Fin 10 bound. The native model records every constructor beside the erased base transport. Source-free offline C and C++ consumers pass 2026 and 2019 checks: accepted and constructed values (Unicode, embedded NUL, 2^100), rejection as the INVALID_ARGUMENT status in C and an Error with that status in C++ naming the parameter and constructor with inputs and outputs unchanged, the second of two checked arguments rejected after the first passed, the Fin bound rejected before the constructor runs, the normalizing constructor's value reaching the export, and 1,000 rejection and recovery cycles. An LD_PRELOAD probe on the C package counts validator, adapter and source dispatch with positive controls: a rejected public value reaches only its validator, never the export; a raw invalid adapter call returns none without reaching the export; and three batches of 20,000 accepted, rejected and late-rejected heap-backed calls keep the resident size flat (20037632, 20037632, 20037632 bytes) while 200,000 deliberately leaked adapter results grow it to 32620544.",
